Subject: Competitive play: RANKED against the opponent by the match's rules
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84

A player signed in to a Recharged profile on the launcher's Competitive page
can accept a test match with another player, by a rule set the WFC server's
admins keep (docs/profiles.md of recharged-wfc-srv). The server pairs both
games in RANKED, where each then finds only the other. Those games, and only
those, play by the match's rules:

- SetupGameFromConfig takes the match's skill level, time or goal limit and
  series length instead of the ranked defaults (mDefaultSettings), and clears
  both teams' Mega Strike flags when the rules have No Mega Strikes;
- Fast terrain and Thunder Island walls apply online when the rules have
  them, next to their offline tweak hooks (0012, 0016);
- the host's GameStart carries the stadium the rules fix, after the original
  random pick, so the network random numbers stay the same.

The port decides at each match's setup, from the lobby's other machine and
the match the launcher's session holds (src/platform/competitive_match.cpp);
a match keeps its answer to the end. Without a session, or against anyone
else, RANKED and every other mode stay retail.

diff --git a/include/mscharged_competitive.h b/include/mscharged_competitive.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ef60b8a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/include/mscharged_competitive.h
@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
+#ifndef MSCHARGED_COMPETITIVE_H
+#define MSCHARGED_COMPETITIVE_H
+
+// Competitive play of the native port (src/platform/competitive_match.cpp in
+// the game module). A player signed in on the launcher's Competitive page
+// with an accepted match plays its RANKED games against that match's
+// opponent by the match's rules; every other game stays retail. Both
+// machines have the same rules (the server pairs them only once both
+// confirmed them), and a match keeps the rules it started with.
+
+#ifdef __cplusplus
+extern "C" {
+#endif
+
+// The gameplay settings of a competitive match (GameplaySettings' values).
+struct MschargedCompetitiveSettings
+{
+    int skill; // GameplaySettings::eSkillLevel
+    int limit; // eGameLimitType
+    int time;  // seconds
+    int goals;
+    int games; // in the series
+};
+
+// At the setup of every match (SetupGameFromConfig): the competitive
+// settings when it is a RANKED match against the opponent, otherwise null.
+// The answer holds until the next match's setup.
+const struct MschargedCompetitiveSettings* mscharged_competitive_begin(void);
+// Whether this match plays with game tweak `tweak` by its competitive rules.
+bool mscharged_competitive_tweak(int tweak);
+// The host's stadium for a RANKED match about to start: the competitive
+// match's when its rules fix one and the other machine is the opponent,
+// otherwise `stadium`.
+int mscharged_competitive_stadium(int stadium);
+
+#ifdef __cplusplus
+}
+#endif
+
+#endif // MSCHARGED_COMPETITIVE_H
+#endif // MSCHARGED_TWEAKS
